cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. No canonical citation format
  has been agreed for this project yet; the fields below are the facts
  confirmed locally (from pyproject.toml and this run's git history), not
  a fully worked-out citation record. hoh is the package, module, and CLI
  that implement the Harness-of-Harness pattern; VeriHarness is the project
  built on that pattern and the name this citation records.
title: "VeriHarness: an evidence-bound Harness-of-Harness for verifiable long-horizon agent development"
version: 0.3.0a1
date-released: "2026-10-07"
# date-released: the date of the documentation checkpoint at which the pre-release is
# cut; the operator may move it if the tag is cut on another day.
# Provenance: this file said `version: 0.1.0` with `date-released: "2026-09-08"`
# until 2026-10-07, when `version` became the pre-release; the date that
# belonged to 0.1.0 does not belong to 0.3.0a1 and is not carried over.
authors:
